# Implementation Plan - Route Duplication Fix & Data Sync

Bhai, aapne ekdum sahi step-by-step workflow samjhaya hai! Ye plan ab aapke bataye steps ke mutabik update kiya gaya hai.

## Proposed Workflow

---

### 1. Stop Services on AWS Server
Sabse pehle hum AWS server par login karke PM2 me chal rahe backend ko stop karenge taaki jab hum data clean kar rahe ho tab koi naya garbage data add na ho jaye.

### 2. Database Cleanup (Deduplication) on AWS
Ek cleanup script chala kar AWS VM par maujood `data.json` me se 4000+ duplicate/kachra routes ko filter aur delete karenge, sirf original unique routes ko preserve karenge.

### 3. Code Fix & Sync
#### [MODIFY] [routeLearning.ts](file:///c:/Users/Azad%20Singh/Desktop/upbus/apps/backend/src/engine/routeLearning.ts)
- Backend code ko update karenge jisme **Bidirectional (Reverse) aur Subset Checking** hogi taaki aage se duplicates banne band ho jayein.
- Ye code Github par push karke, AWS server par `git pull` se update kiya jayega.

### 4. Restart Services
Fix apply hone ke baad, AWS VM par PM2 ko dobara start (run) karenge jisse backend fresh aur clean data ke sath chalu ho jayega.

### 5. Download `data.json` to Local Computer
Jo bilkul clean aur unique `data.json` AWS par banegi, usko download karke aapke local project folder mein paste kar denge taaki aapka local computer bhi bilkul Live data ke sath sync ho jaye!

---

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **User Action Required**
> Ye saare steps (PM2 stop karna, data clean karna, file download karna) karne ke liye mujhe aapke AWS Server me SSH login karna hoga.
> Purana IP kaam nahi kar raha hai, isliye **kripya AWS Console se naya Public IP Address (IPv4) yahan bhejein!** Jaise hi IP milega, main ye saare steps turant shuru kar dunga.
